# Unity CLI only

For any Unity work in this project, use **only the Unity CLI** (`unity`). Do not use third-party Unity MCP packages, the deprecated in-Editor AI Assistant MCP server, or ad-hoc Editor automation outside the CLI.

## Preferred interface

Prefer shell commands over MCP (faster, fewer tokens):

```bash
unity status
unity command
unity command <name> [args...]
unity command eval '/* C# */'
```

Pass `--project-path D:\Unity-Projects\Aiming-Archery` when more than one Editor may be open. From this repo's cwd, auto-detection is usually enough.

## When the Editor is running

If `unity status` shows this project as `ready`, drive the live Editor via CLI instead of hand-editing `.unity` / `.prefab` / `.asset` YAML.

Requires `com.unity.pipeline` (already in this project). Recover Safe Mode / connection failures with `unity pipeline list` and compile fixes — do not fall back to blind scene-file edits.

## MCP

Cursor may already be configured with the CLI MCP (`unity mcp` in `~/.cursor/mcp.json`). That is allowed because it is the Unity CLI server. Do not add or prefer a different Unity MCP. Prefer `unity command` / `unity status` when shell is available.

